text:
The moon is riding on the wings of morning,

 And the golden horn is calling me;

 The sun is going down and I am riding,

 A rider on his way to see;

In silence, and in sorrow,
I watch your footsteps fall;

Through tears I see you pass me,
And hear my heart grow small;

For that one love alone is left—
One lonely moment's call.

In that one day, my Lord, so full of grace,
 My soul to heaven was raised and carried away ;
 That is indeed most blessed;

 And as I lay within its bosom there :—

 In all thy creatures then 1 saw thee, O my God !

The night is full, and her eyes are bright;
 She smiles when she sees me come to-night ;

She hath some charms by magic arts to raise,
 Some graces not her own, but what she owes,
   Which makes them much more lovely than they are :

The light, my friend, and the dark we must not shun;
Let the shadows be our bedfellows, for they are true;

In their presence our dreams may come to us
Without fear or hesitation from a starless sky;
